# Allow-list for the Hermes memories backup repository.
#
# This file is installed as `.gitignore` inside $HERMES_BACKUP_REPO by
# hermes-backup.sh. It exists because that repository lives INSIDE the agent's
# home directory (/opt/data), which also holds config.yaml, config/auth.json and
# .env. A plain `git add -A` there sweeps all of it into a repo that has a
# GitHub remote — which is exactly what used to happen (534 tracked files).
#
# Deny by default, then re-allow only the agent's memory files. Keep this in
# sync with BACKED_UP_FILES in hermes-backup.sh.
*

!.gitignore
!MEMORY.md
!USER.md
